# Slice 293 (FORMAL-DEFAULT-FORMS): a formal whose written default is an expression, not a literal.  The translator
# builds a default only from a literal of the formal's own primitive type -- a limit of the builder in this phase, not a
# norm (Codex's 293 review: what the general construction makes of such a written form is open).  The default is not
# built, and a call that omits the formal is refused at translation (a call that gives the argument translates, probe
# p293g).
fn: d (int: a 2 + 3) int
    return: a
end: d
int: code 7
if: d() != 5
    code := 81
---
send: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
